 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Parallel Normal:** If the surfel normal $\vec{n}$ is parallel to the reference vector $\vec{a}=(0,1,0)$, the cross product $\vec{a} \times \vec{n}$ yields a zero vector. The algorithm must detect this and switch $\vec{a}$ to $(0,0,-1)$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Artifacts:** Sharp square-shaped boundary artifacts may appear due to alpha-blending and rendering order. Disabling depth buffer operations can mitigate this but introduces other sorting issues [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Isotropy Assumption:** The method assumes isotropic surfels. If anisotropic scaling is required, the scale matrix $S$ must be modified to use distinct $r_x$ and $r_y$ values [S1, unofficial].
