 ## Operating characteristics
-
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of surfels, as each surfel is processed independently as a primitive.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ to store surfel attributes. Video memory is the primary constraint for buffer sizes [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Leverages hardware-accelerated geometry instancing and rasterization. Simple to implement on standard graphics pipelines.
-*   **Limitations:** Prone to sharp boundary artifacts if not handled. Requires careful handling of the normal-to-basis conversion to avoid degeneracy.
-*   **When to use:** When rendering scanned point clouds or meshes where surface orientation is known and hardware rasterization is preferred over ray tracing.
