 ## Background
-
-Surfel rendering was introduced as a technique to render scanned 4D media using hardware-accelerated geometry instancing. The method treats surfels as oriented, texture-mapped quadrilaterals aligned to surface curvature [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address the limitations of traditional billboard rendering by providing surface-aligned primitives that better represent the underlying geometry [S1, unofficial].
